<spell-notebook "button theming" original="/components/ui/ui-button.html">
	<header level="1">
		Button
		<header>A button indicates a possible user action.</header>
	</header>
	<button-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<html>
			<ui-menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
				<ui-item link="#tokens">Tokens</ui-item>
				<ui-item link="#themes">Themes</ui-item>
			</ui-menu>
		</html>
	</section>

	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Theme a button with the public `--ui-button-*` tokens.
			Set one on the element, on any ancestor (a group, a toolbar, `:root`),
			or on the inner box through `::part(button)`.

			- They inherit into the shadow root, where the sheet reads each through a private alias,
			  so nothing inside blocks them.
			- Set on a `<ui-buttons>`, they reach every button in the group.
		</markdown>
		<markdown>
			```css
			/* every button on the page */
			:root {
			  --ui-button-radius: 999px;
			}
			/* one region */
			.toolbar {
			  --ui-button-padding-inline: 1.5em;
			}
			/* one kind, on its box */
			ui-button.cta::part(button) {
			  --ui-button-background: var(--ui-yellow);
			}
			```
		</markdown>
		<message state="info" size="small">
			<markdown>
				Variations build on the base tokens:

				- `compact` scales your `--ui-button-padding-block`.
				- `circular` replaces the radius, whatever you set.

				To restyle a variation itself, target it with plain properties:

				```css
				/* less round */
				ui-button[appearance~="circular"]::part(button) {
				  border-radius: 0.5em;
				}
				```

				Never set the private names, `--_ui-*` and `--_button-*`:  they're the sheet's own plumbing.
			</markdown>
		</message>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</markdown>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-button" playground>
				<ui-button>Follow</ui-button>
			</ui-docs-tokens>
		</html>
	</section>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			The theme menu above picks the theme for every page of the site:  Spell, Glass, Fruity or Merlot,
			each restyling this component through its tokens.
		</markdown>
	</section>
</spell-notebook>
